{
  "id": "Compound::DB00757 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Dolasetron exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2d6, which is a key enzyme involved in the metabolism of various substrates. This binding leads to Cyp2d6 participating in multiple metabolic pathways, including aromatase activity and tamoxifen metabolism. These pathways are ultimately linked to Cyp3a4, suggesting a mechanistic pathway through which Dolasetron influences Cyp3a4. The evidence from the three paths collectively supports a direct interaction between Dolasetron and Cyp3a4, mediated through Cyp2d6. The shared involvement of Cyp2d6 in different metabolic processes, coupled with the direct participation of Cyp3a4 in these pathways, indicates a plausible and biologically relevant mechanism. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Cyp2d6 as a critical mediator in the relationship between Dolasetron and Cyp3a4, emphasizing the importance of enzyme activity in drug metabolism and its potential impact on drug efficacy and toxicity.",
